    "body": "Fixes #8110.\n\n- Gate condition: `always() && !contains(needs.*.result, 'cancelled')` → `!cancelled()` for `ci-early-success`, `ci-success` and `sanitizers-success`. When a needed job is cancelled (for example by `timeout-minutes`), the gate now runs and `FAIL`, which already treats `cancelled` as failure, becomes 1, instead of the gate being skipped (a required check treats skipped as passing). When the whole run is cancelled (e.g. superseded by a newer push), `cancelled()` is true and the gate is still skipped, as before.\n- Add `file-changes` to the gates' `needs`, so a failed change detection fails the gate instead of only causing skips. On `workflow_dispatch` and tags `file-changes` is skipped, which `FAIL` accepts.\n\nChecked in a test repository: after a needed job hit its timeout, the dependent gate saw `needs.<job>.result == 'cancelled'` with `cancelled()` false, so it runs under the new condition.\n\nAs discussed in #8110: with this change the Windows ARM jobs that currently time out will make `ci-success` fail. Those tests may need to be excluded separately until the runner issue is resolved; I left that out of this PR so it only changes the gate logic.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Vx41jkTKgrWAx3u5A78K5p",
